
This directory is intended for PlatformIO Test Runner and project tests.

Unit Testing is a software testing method by which individual units of
source code, sets of one or more MCU program modules together with associated
control data, usage procedures, and operating procedures, are tested to
determine whether they are fit for use. Unit testing finds problems early
in the development cycle.

More information about PlatformIO Unit Testing:
- https://docs.platformio.org/en/latest/advanced/unit-testing/index.html

The test plan covers 90+ individual test cases across five sections:
Section 1 — ESP32 Unit Tests (PlatformIO/Unity, all AI-generatable): Graphics encoding byte-for-byte correctness, WiFiTransport buffer accumulation and flush, ActiveTransport switching, back-channel frame parser including fragmentation and resync, BLE TX ring buffer wrap-around and overflow.
Section 2 — iPhone Unit Tests (XCTest, all AI-generatable): GFXCommandStream frame reassembly including byte-by-byte delivery, iPhoneGFXRenderer pixel output verification, GFXDisplayView flush buffering and auto-flush timer, TransportMonitor state machine and all three WiFi diagnosis paths.
Section 3 — Integration Tests: WiFi and BLE connection/data flow on real hardware, transport switching priority and fallback. Python serial assertion script approach described.
Section 4 — System/E2E Tests: Full telemetry pipeline, 30-minute stability, physical TFT vs iPhone sync.
Section 5 — Corner Cases: Eight regression tests tagged [REGRESSION] for the specific bugs fixed during this session (heap corruption, reconnect loop, clientSpace gate, buffer reset), plus protocol boundary values, heartbeat edge cases, and memory stress.
Appendix: Four copy-paste AI prompt templates — ESP32 unit test, iPhone XCTest, Python serial log asserter, and GPS NMEA simulator — each designed to be dropped into a new AI session with architecture.md as context.
